# crease.part -- Rounds of a slot across a crease of the face they meet
# Copyright (c) 2026 Jakob Kastelic

# A slab whose top is flat ahead of y = 15 and leans down 1 degree behind
# it, and a slot along y through the crease, its walls drafted 1.5
# degrees.  The rounds of the slot edges along the top meet in a miter
# at the crease, which stays sharp; at the ends of the slot the rounds
# meet those on the end faces, and there a piece of the plane of each
# miter closes the gap between them.
profile fr along y 0 -10 0 40 -10 0 40 0 0 0 0 0
extrude front from 0 to 15 fr
profile bk along y -100 -10 0 140 -10 0 140 0 0 -100 0 0
extrude back from 15 to 30 bk draft 1
union slab front back
profile sl along y 15 -5 0 25 -5 0 25 1 0 15 1 0
extrude slot from 35 to -5 sl draft 1.5
subtract part slab slot
round 0.3 slot front
round 0.3 slot back
